{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1526091-threat-null-s-void-engineers","id":1526091,"title":"Threat Null's Void Engineers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-11-28T17:13:24-08:00","id":1526091,"title":"Threat Null's Void Engineers","content":"My take on the Threat Null counterpart to the Void Engineers: it doesn't exist. <br /> <br /> My reasoning: the thing that caused the other Technocrats who were lost to Disembodiment to become unified factions was the Conditioning they had been subjected to, which had the metaphysical effect of bonding them together in a way that roughly mirrored their Convention-based identities; and that, in turn, resulted in their new spirit-forms being extreme stereotypes of those organizations. This is why you don't see Traditionist counterparts to Threat Null: it's not that Superstitionists don't undergo Disembodiment; but rather, the types of spirits they become are based on the individual mages' identities rather than the identities of whatever groups they may or may not have signed on with. <br /> <br /> The Void Engineers have a Methodology devoted to undoing Conditioning. Originally, this was merely because the VEs disapproved of the practice; but after the advent of Threat Null, it became clear to them of the exceedingly practical drawback that being Conditioned makes you vulnerable to Threat Null recruitment. This redoubled their opposition to Conditioning. So now, they're no longer <i>just</i> removing any Conditioning that new recruits may have undergone; they're also doing what they can to try to convince the rest of the Conventions to abandon the practice, too. Not that there's much they <i>can</i> do, because they can't exactly show a Conditioned Technocrat evidence of Threat Null and what happens when a Conditioned Technocrat encounters them; but they're looking for ways. <br /> <br /> But let that sink in: Void Engineers aren't Conditioned. And because they're not Conditioned, Disembodiment doesn't turn them into extreme stereotypes of their Convention. So there <i>is </i>no Threat Null counterpart to the Void Engineers. <br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-29T01:14:13-08:00","id":1526106,"title":"","content":"You got a like from me. Although it suggests to me that something similar is possible for some of the other Mage groups. The Templar Knights and the Batini have their own styles of group think. I could see both groups as vulnerable. The Batini, because of their, &quot;we understand this just do what we say when we tell you&quot; worldview, strike me as being as vulnerable as the NWO or the Syndicate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-29T01:26:51-08:00","id":1526107,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking that Technocratic Conditioning goes deeper than that. I mean, even the Void Engineers, in their post-Storm militarization, have taken on a more conformist style than they had before the Storm; but they don't have Conditioning, and aren't vulnerable to Threat Null \u201crecruitment\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-30T03:25:08-08:00","id":1526172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1526091-threat-null-s-void-engineers#post1526091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Void Engineers have a Methodology devoted to undoing Conditioning... Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>I like it a lot; it's in retrospect really obvious, and it's odd that it's not given as a possibility.<br /> <br /> That said, if you go back to the original VE book, that's not what they were doing then. ECTA originally didn't dare actually undo conditioning (under threat of an NWO investigation), they merely altered it slightly to make members loyal to the Convention rather than the NWO. That's presumably why it's not given as a possibility, whilst it's suggested that the Threat Null VEs may have simply wandered off on their own.<br /> <br /> Then again, it's also a little odd that the Revised VE book doesn't bring up this big change of policy by ECTA; so maybe it was meant as a retcon?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-30T06:16:05-08:00","id":1526182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because Technocracy agents so often face off with Things Man Was Not Meant to Know, the NSC also has a secondary purpose: Providing mental health treatment for their fellow Technocrats. Called the <i>Descartes Institute of Mental Health</i>, this medical division works within normal hospitals and Void Engineer Constructs to restore sanity to damaged operatives, install mental defenses against insidious psychic influences and raw trauma; and (unbeknownst to the NWO) safeguards against and/or undo Social Processing for Void Engineer operatives. This last procedure indicates the sustain many VEs holds for the Order's PsychOps and the oppressive hold of Control and the Inner Circle. Although they may have adopted a more militaristic approach in recent years, and work hand-in-glove with earthbound Black Suits, the Void Engineers prefer to make their own decisions based upon their own loyalties, not to have those decisions and loyalties implanted into them by a dubious third party with decidedly sinister goals<br /> <br /> <b>Technocracy Reloaded</b>, pp. 162\u2013163 </div> </div> </div>DIMH isn't about changing loyalties from the NWO to the VEs; it's about removing the forced compliance entirely. And what \u201cconditionibg\u201d they implement is designed to maximize the operative's agency, making it harder for anyone to make them do anything against their free will. That's why Technocrats under NWO Conditioning are vulnerable to Threat Null and VEs who have been treated by DIMH <i>aren't.</i><br /> <br /> This isn't new. <b>Guide to the Technocracy</b> essays that \u201cthe <b>Enforcement Training and Conditioning Agency</b> (ETCA) implants safety conditioning into space-bound personnel (and deactivates unwanted NWO conditioning\u201d (p.119); the original <b>Technocracy: Void Engineers</b> book talks about how the ETCA isn't about stomping out free will the way regular Conditioning is, but it's more aimed at making sure operatives don't freak out when faced with extra dimensional entities, and reversing Conditioning (too much to quote succinctly; p.27). And <b>Convention Book: Void Engineers</b> says that \u201cA division of the DIMH \u2026 oversees deprogramming Cadets in our colleges. This further cements their professional distain for the NWO; they constantly have to dig damaging mental conditioning out of the minds of young people, whose only crime is possessing a desire to learn and a temperament c given to wandering. Once conditioning has been broken, the ETCA then proceeds to implant safety training into the Cadets' minds. This includes buffering their psyches against the shock and trauma of encountering dangerous alien entities. \u2026 This is not another form of social and mental control. It allows Void Engineers to make the best possible decisions with a clear mind, while mainstream Technocratic conditioning seeks to control those decisions.\u201d (p.46)<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 11-30-2023, 09:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-30T09:27:43-08:00","id":1526186,"title":"","content":"Maybe I wasn't clear. I wasn't disputing about the present VEs, I was meaning that they seem to have had different policies pre-Anomaly (ie. in their original book).<br /> <br /> Now, a character on p 27 says that they reverse conditioning, but the actual magic section on page 45 describes the effect:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Usually, the Conditioning is never completely removed, only subverted. The complexity of this Effect lies in its subtlety - if Technocrats appeared to have their NWO Conditioning reversed completely, an extensive investigation would begin. However, if certain small but important points of the Conditioning are altered, the operative becomes loyal to the Void Engineers, rather than to the New World Order.\u200b </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-30T14:52:24-08:00","id":1526192,"title":"","content":"Fair enough. However, no subsequent book reiterates that claim. <b>Guide to the Technocracy</b> doesn't even <i>have </i>a deprogramming rote in it; and both <b>Convention Book Void Engineers </b>and <b>Technocracy Reloaded </b>go all in on the idea that the Void Engineers deprogram their personnel as much as they can. The Convention Book, in particular, cites the social programming of the rest of the Technocracy as the reason why they succumb to Threat Null so easily, making the deprogramming not <i>just </i>a way to express contempt for the NWO, but also something that <i>must be done </i>to avoid an existential crisis. And even in the <i>first </i>book, there are lots of references to the VEs despising the NWO and doing what they can to oppose their excesses. The \u201cBig Joke\u201d is another example. <br /> <br /> Personally, I chalk up the <b>Technocracy: Void Engineers</b> reference you gave to the same thing as how the <b>Technocracy: <b>Progenitor</b>s</b> book has a reference in it to them working on a project to purge Avatars from humanity: an early edition bit of weirdness that largely got ignored later on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}